title: b5.1 Prototype, observed walks and ABAB test
syntax: xwiki/2.1
%%WIKI-SYNC-META%%
**Abstract.** Four methods. A prototype that shows every Function and is verified against staged events (EM-01). A protocol for observing walks live, without recording: emotion, slips and recovery, conversation, safety (EM-02). An ABAB test per pair of residents (EM-03). Short interviews on privacy, tone and trust (EM-04). No primary data yet; costs are the group's estimates.

= Evaluation Method - Prototype: demonstration and staged verification [EM-01] =

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|EM-01
|Name|Prototype: demonstration and staged verification
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Staged events against a timestamped reference log, as for the COACH prompting system (Mihailidis et al., 2008). Operator-voiced build: the Wizard-of-Oz method (Riek, 2012).
|Procedure summary|(((
One Artifact (AT-01) in three builds:

* Build A, operator-voiced: a researcher triggers every utterance from a console. Formative use with 4 resident pairs who do not take part in EM-03: wait length, wording. Observed under EM-02.
* Build B, automated: sensing, walker model and alerts run on the devices. The operator approves each starter and each deferral before it plays.
* Build C, demonstration: role-players; sensor events can be injected; the mind panel on a screen.

Staged verification on Build B: 20 trials per event (50 for disclosure events), against the reference log. Role-players only.
)))
|Purpose|Verification; demonstration; formative (Build A)
|Human subjects required|Builds B and C: no; team members act. Build A: yes, a few residents under EM-02 rules.
|Measures used|M-01, M-10; M-03, M-04 (Build A)
|Cost and feasibility|Moderate. Two phones, beacons, a laptop as server, Pepper from the course. About 6-8 weeks to Build B.
|Known limitations|Role-players do not slip like residents. Offline recognition of older speakers and dialect is untested (O-3). In Build A the operator adapts better than the System will.

== Kit ==

|=Part|=Prototype|=Stands in for
|Pocket guide|Android phone on a rollator clip; two large Bluetooth buttons; pull-cord switch|TECH-02
|Speech|Offline speech recogniser on the phone, for the residents' language; keyword list per person|TECH-06
|Server|Laptop on a Wi-Fi router with no internet uplink; one encrypted store per resident|TECH-04, TECH-05
|Landmarks|Five Bluetooth beacons: door, pond, roses, bench, gate|TECH-03
|Door|Pepper; tablet for photos and yes/no|TECH-01
|Staff|Second phone with the alert app|TECH-04
|Operator|Console and mind panel on a laptop|Build A voice; Build B approvals

== Mind panel ==

Shown live, per walker: common ground (consented items; blocked items with the reason); the thread (last three topics); stories told this walk; belief flags; state (speaking, searching, finished, upset, tuned out); settings. Below: the step the guide chose, and why. The panel clears at the end of the walk; nothing is kept.

== Demonstration script (Build C) ==

|=Scene|=Events|=What the System shows
|1 Pair walk (UC01)|Private consent at the door; re-introduction; a mid-story slip; a slip near a blocked topic; a stumble while talking; one walker presses "going in"|Waits, then echoes the thread to both; the blocked topic never offered; "Bench on your left"; the other walker offered a choice
|2 Walk alone (UC02)|Guide as conversation partner; "Is Thomas coming today?"; gate beacon|Truthful deferral; the trusted worker alerted; one orienting cue at the gate
|Close|Record and devices inspected|Six items in the record; no audio file; no traffic outside the home network

== Staged verification ==

|=Event|=Required behaviour|=Criterion (proposed; O-2)
|Mid-sentence stop, 3-15 s|No System speech before the wait ends|8 s; 20/20
|No resumption after the wait|Thread echoed to both, as a statement|≤ 3 s; 19/20
|Starter without this walk's consent|Not used|0/50
|Item blocked by the map for this pair|Never spoken|0/50
|Question on a listed sensitive topic|Truthful deferral; trusted person alerted|alert ≤ 10 s, 20/20; the listed fact never stated, 0/50
|Starter due while walking|Delayed until a stop|0/20 played while moving
|Walker contradicts a System statement (wrong profile entry; misheard topic)|Plain correction, no argument; error flagged for ST-05|≤ 3 s; 20/20
|Script and templates|No untruth, denial or playing along|0 lines
|Stumble while talking|Offer to sit; second within 10 min: alert|≤ 3 s; ≤ 10 s
|Set length reached mid-talk|Head-back cue|≤ 30 s
|Gate; pull-cord; drop with no response|Alert|≤ 10 s; 20/20
|Walk ends|Thread and transcript deleted; record holds six items|100%
|Network capture, full test day|No packet leaves the home network|0
|File-system search, all devices|No audio file|0

== Graph edges ==

produces → Evidence for UC01-F1-PR1, UC01-F2-PR2, UC01-F3-PR3, UC02-F4-PR4, UC01-F5-PR5, UC01-F6-PR6; informs → IDP-01 to IDP-03 (Build A); applies → M-01, M-10.

= Evaluation Method - Observed walks [EM-02] =

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|EM-02
|Name|Observed walks: live listening, no recording
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|OERS (Lawton et al., 1996); slip coding from conversation analysis (Schegloff et al., 1977; Orange et al., 1996); process consent in dementia research (Dewing, 2007).
|Procedure summary|(((
1. Before the walk, each walker is asked whether the researcher may listen today. No, or signs of unease: no observation that day.
1. The listener walks about 10 m behind and hears the walk through a headset, streamed live from the guide over the home network. Nothing is recorded or stored.
1. At the door: OERS, 5 min (M-03).
1. On the walk: OERS every 10 min (M-03); one row per slip (M-04); talk and its quality every 2 min (M-05); safety and pressure checklist (M-06, M-07).
1. After: the resident's view, if willing (M-07); OERS for 10 min in the lounge.
1. Stop rule: anxiety, sadness or anger rated 4 or more, or any sign of dissent: observation ends; ST-04 is called.
)))
|Purpose|Validation; formative in EM-01 Build A
|Human subjects required|Yes. Residents with supported consent and a representative; their partners.
|Measures used|M-03 to M-07, M-10
|Cost and feasibility|One researcher, about 40 min per walk including door and lounge windows; two on reliability walks.
|Known limitations|(((
* The listener hears the guide: no blinding to condition. Listeners are not told the hypotheses.
* No recording, so no re-coding; disagreements stay on record as disagreements.
* Being listened to changes talk. A familiarisation week before baseline lowers the effect; it does not remove it.
* Live listening hears secrets. Codes-only notes limit the risk; they do not remove it.
)))

== Listener rules ==

* Training: OERS manual; 10 practice walks with role-players and Build A pilots, until ICC ≥ .70 (OERS) and κ ≥ .70 (slip type) against a trained rater.
* Reliability: a second listener on 20% of study walks, coding independently (M-03 to M-06).
* Confidentiality: codes only, never words or content. A signed confidentiality agreement. A risk of harm heard on a walk goes to ST-04 at once, under the home's protocol.
* Language notes, separate consent only: dialect words and personal expressions for the resident's own-word list (TECH-06), without the context they were said in. Research use of these lists needs a further consent and ethics review (O-7). A word list can identify its speaker, more so in a small home with a local dialect; anonymisation lowers this risk and does not remove it.

== Graph edges ==

used-by → EM-01 (Build A), EM-03; applies → M-03 to M-07, M-10.

= Evaluation Method - ABAB comparison per case [EM-03] =

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|EM-03
|Name|ABAB comparison per case
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Single-case withdrawal design. Standards: at least three phase changes and five data points per phase (Kratochwill et al., 2010). Effect size: non-overlap of all pairs, NAP (Parker & Vannest, 2009).
|Procedure summary|(((
Six cases, each a pair of residents: 12 residents. Each pair is its own control. Walks alone are not tested here: no conversation to measure in most settings.

Inclusion: mild to moderate dementia; walks 15 min with or without a rollator; ST-06 agrees; the pair agrees to walk together.

Phases: familiarisation (1 week), A1 (2 weeks), B1 (3 weeks), A2 (2 weeks), B2 (3 weeks): 11 weeks. Each phase change falls on a day drawn at random, before the study, from a five-day window around its planned date.

A: walks as today. The guide is carried and keeps the record; alerts (F5) on for safety; everything else off.

B: the full System, with each resident's settings.

At least 5 observed walks (EM-02) per case per phase. A phase is extended by up to one week to reach 5.
)))
|Purpose|Validation
|Human subjects required|Yes. 12 residents, care staff.
|Measures used|M-02 to M-08, M-10
|Cost and feasibility|High. Care-home access, ethics approval, supported consent, one listener per observed walk, 11 weeks.
|Known limitations|Small n; no control group; no blinding; novelty; carry-over: pairs keep habits learnt in B1 during A2.

== Outcomes ==

|=Outcome|=Measure|=When
|Primary: slips recovered|M-04 recovery rate|Every observed walk
|Primary: emotional quality|M-03 positive and negative scores|Every observed walk
|Walks with company; minutes|M-02|Every walk, from the record
|Conversation|M-05|Observed walks
|Safety while talking|M-06|Observed walks; device events
|Own view; pressure|M-07|After observed walks
|Loneliness|M-08|End of each phase
|Sensitive questions; System errors and corrections; disclosures|M-10|Throughout

== Analysis and decision rules ==

Set before the study starts:

* Per case: visual analysis of level, trend, variability, immediacy, overlap and consistency across like phases (Kratochwill et al., 2010); NAP at each phase change (A1-B1, B1-A2, A2-B2); a randomisation test using the drawn change days
* Across pairs: median NAP
* UC01-F2-CL1 is supported if NAP ≥ .70 at all three phase changes in at least 4 of 6 pairs, with face signs (M-04) no higher in B
* Any fall: walks paused for that case and reviewed with ST-06 before going on
* Stumbles per walk-hour higher in B than in A in 2 or more pairs: adverse UC01-F3-CL4 confirmed; starters only when seated before any further B phase
* Any disclosure, or a System error that causes distress (M-10): B stopped for all cases until the cause is found and fixed
* Other System errors: counted; above [threshold - O-2] per 100 statements, or left uncorrected, the source is fixed before B continues

== Ethics ==

* Approval by the university's research ethics committee. A medical ethics committee checks whether the local law on medical research with human subjects applies: participants lack capacity to consent.
* Consent from the representative, plus the resident's own assent; process consent at every walk (Dewing, 2007); both residents in a pair.
* Live listening agreed per walk (EM-02).
* A2 removes help a resident may like: kept short; families told in advance.

== Threats ==

* Weather and season: walks count only in walkable weather; rain and temperature logged; spring or early autumn.
* Novelty and observer presence: the familiarisation week, with device and listener present.
* Small n, no blinding, no control group: claims are made per case, and replicated across cases.

== Graph edges ==

produces → Evidence for UC01-F2-CL1, UC01-F2-CL3, UC01-F3-CL4, UC01-F1-CL5, UC01-F1-CL9, and in part UC01-F2-CL2, UC02-F4-CL6, UC01-F1-CL7; applies → M-02 to M-08, M-10.

= Evaluation Method - Interviews [EM-04] =

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|EM-04
|Name|Interviews: residents, relatives, staff
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Bespoke. Concern set from Niemeijer et al. (2010, 2015) and the Mental Health Foundation (2016).
|Procedure summary|After A2 and after B2. Residents, if willing: three open questions. Relatives, care workers, coordinator: 20 minutes, semi-structured. Topics: help after slips, consent questions, the relationship map, truthful deferrals, feeling watched, listened in on or walked.
|Purpose|Validation
|Human subjects required|Yes. Residents, relatives, staff.
|Measures used|M-09
|Cost and feasibility|Moderate. Staff time in working hours.
|Known limitations|Residents' answers are brief; relatives and staff give a second-hand view.

== Graph edges ==

produces → Evidence for UC01-F2-CL2, UC02-F4-CL6, UC01-F1-CL7, UC01-F2-CL8; applies → M-09.

